@* EPIC 35 Sprint 35.1-R2 (OWNER correction): shared authenticated-workspace Hero composition, used by
   ProfileHome, Wallet and DailyHome so the three primary authenticated surfaces share one visual
   language instead of three independent ad-hoc wrappers (Profile and Wallet had each already grown
   their own, slightly different, one-off attempt at this). Mirrors the existing
   Components/Pages/Institutional/Components/InstitutionalPageShell.razor pattern (BeeDayHero + a body
   region) applied to the authenticated context — the difference is this component owns ONLY the
   full-workspace-width Hero surface; each page keeps rendering its own body markup/width rules
   exactly as before, as a sibling rendered after this component, not as a ChildContent slot here, so
   no page's existing body composition needs to change shape.

   BeeDayHero remains the single shared visual Hero primitive — this is a thin structural wrapper
   around it, not a competing component (LabBoundaryTests guards against a future duplicate). The
   wrapper element below is required, not decorative: BeeDayHero renders as a sibling of each page's
   own body container (.product-home, .wallet-page, .dashboard-page), not nested inside it, so a
   page-scoped ::deep CSS rule needs an element carrying THIS component's own scope attribute to
   attach to — without it the rule compiles to a scope attribute the hero's actual <header> never
   carries and silently matches nothing (found the hard way against ProfileHome's first, page-local
   version of this fix — see WorkspaceHero.razor.css). *@
<div class="workspace-hero">
    <BeeDayHero Compact="true"
                Surface="Surface"
                Eyebrow="@Eyebrow"
                Title="@Title"
                Subtitle="@Subtitle">
        <PrimaryAction>@PrimaryAction</PrimaryAction>
    </BeeDayHero>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public string? Eyebrow { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Subtitle { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? PrimaryAction { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Defaults to Cor0 — the same brand-primary surface Wallet's hero (EPIC 27 Sprint 27.11)
    /// already used, kept as the one coherent authenticated-hero surface across Profile/Wallet/Daily
    /// per the OWNER's explicit direction ("coherent surface treatment... unless there is documented
    /// Design System reason for route-specific surface differences") — no such reason exists in this
    /// Sprint, so every current consumer uses the default rather than passing Surface explicitly.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public BeeDayPaletteToken Surface { get; set; } = BeeDayPaletteToken.Cor0;
}
